  "decisions": [
    {
      "decision_ref": "gxa_a34306707bc117b60a45cb04479c5f48c9e24f05139561b75516f09dc9749d5e",
      "turn_id": "01a21ed5-cd24-7662-87c4-d46c4c5be0e2",
      "rationale": "The deposited covale2 row is the only difference between the files. Use matched methods on both inputs to measure how the edit affects the explicit topology count and model coverage.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "gxa_01m8fdbhmakbwwwe0c",
        "gxa_01m8fdbhn2jacc87v1"
      ],
      "ops": [
        "open_branch",
        "add_node",
        "add_node",
        "add_node",
        "add_node"
      ],
      "outcome": "adopted"
    },
    {
      "decision_ref": "gxa_5c13c5d0d91f65a96dd7eb75e2a96036df270653a9ee3fda89e28fe5c9cc0ff9",
      "turn_id": "01a21ed8-a4c9-76c3-a21d-9c593b72a7f7",
      "rationale": "Deleting the deposited _struct_conn row covale2 reproduces the complete derivative byte for byte. The row links chain A GLN 8 C to DAR 1 N. Both files have the same _atom_site table, PDB accession and primary citation. The inventory module exhausted its allowance and reported no findings. Keep the paired macrocycle and backbone measurements already commissioned. Their outputs will provide the explicit closure count, mapped model count, model-one terminal distance and backbone coverage for each representation of this single NMR deposition.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "gxa_01m8fdbhmakbwwwe0c",
        "gxa_01m8fdbhn2jacc87v1",
        "gxa_b9b04e79c234fdd337b5e75aff0779ed5c831156af59d894c83ae9e19fc7b8d6"
      ],
      "ops": [],
      "outcome": "maintained"
    },
    {
      "decision_ref": "gxa_a1aa1c3d7864b7dd4d4c8cdc2f838813c47e4d512ee7d7885d4af91d6be0f63a",
      "turn_id": "01a21eda-6764-74e0-9dd4-32315059a640",
      "rationale": "Use the deposited _struct_conn record for the explicit topology count. In chain A, covale2 links the GLN 8 carbonyl C to the DAR 1 backbone N. The original closure count is {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh986x2mj3jat:declared_closure}} and the derivative count is {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh99j68cpt4bc:declared_closure}}. Removing that single row reproduces the derivative byte for byte, including its entire _atom_site table. The terminal atoms map in {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh986x2mj3jat:mapped_models}}/{{metric:gxa_01m8fdh986x2mj3jat:model_count}} original models and {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh99j68cpt4bc:mapped_models}}/{{metric:gxa_01m8fdh99j68cpt4bc:model_count}} derivative models. The first-model C–N distances are {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh986x2mj3jat:model_1_distance_A}} and {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh99j68cpt4bc:model_1_distance_A}}, respectively. First-model residue coverage is {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh9ccpmq5kprr:coordinate_coverage}} and {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh9hx98fkvf5q:coordinate_coverage}}, with {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh9ccpmq5kprr:ca_count}} and {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh9hx98fkvf5q:ca_count}} Cα sites and {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh9ccpmq5kprr:complete_backbones}} and {{metric:gxa_01m8fdh9hx98fkvf5q:complete_backbones}} complete backbones. Substituting the derivative would miss the explicitly recorded closure. The files describe one published solution NMR ensemble. The deletion supplies no evidence of ring opening.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "gxa_01m8fdbhmakbwwwe0c",
        "gxa_01m8fdbhn2jacc87v1",
        "gxa_01m8fdh986x2mj3jat",
        "gxa_01m8fdh99j68cpt4bc",
        "gxa_01m8fdh9ccpmq5kprr",
        "gxa_01m8fdh9hx98fkvf5q"
      ],
      "ops": [
        "close_run"
      ],
      "outcome": "adopted"
    }
  ],
